Spring Data JPA

==========================================================
PROJECT NAME
==========================================================

Country CRUD using Spring Boot, Spring Data JPA and MySQL

==========================================================
OBJECTIVE
==========================================================

The objective of this project is to learn the implementation of
Spring Data JPA with MySQL by performing CRUD (Create, Read,
Update and Delete) operations on the Country table and
understanding the concepts of repositories, transactions,
entity mapping and Hibernate.

==========================================================
HANDS-ON COMPLETED
==========================================================

Hands-on 1
-----------
Spring Data JPA Quick Example
- Connected Spring Boot with MySQL.
- Configured Spring Data JPA.
- Retrieved all countries using findAll().

Hands-on 2
-----------
Hibernate XML Configuration Walkthrough
- Studied Hibernate XML configuration.
- Understood SessionFactory, Session, Transaction,
  beginTransaction(), commit(), rollback(),
  save(), get(), delete() and createQuery().list().

Hands-on 3
-----------
Hibernate Annotation Configuration Walkthrough
- Studied Hibernate Annotation configuration.
- Understood @Entity, @Table, @Id,
  @GeneratedValue, @Column and Hibernate configuration.

Hands-on 4
-----------
Difference between JPA, Hibernate and Spring Data JPA
- Studied the differences between
  JPA, Hibernate and Spring Data JPA.
- Understood repository-based implementation
  compared to traditional Hibernate.

Hands-on 5
-----------
Get All Countries
- Retrieved all country records using
  countryRepository.findAll().

Hands-on 6
-----------
Find Country by Code
- Created CountryNotFoundException.
- Implemented findCountryByCode().
- Used findById() to retrieve a country.
- Implemented @Transactional.

Hands-on 7
-----------
Add Country
- Added a new country using
  countryRepository.save().
- Verified the inserted record
  in MySQL database.

Hands-on 8
-----------
Update Country
- Updated an existing country's name.
- Retrieved the country using findById().
- Saved updated entity using save().
- Verified updated data in MySQL.

Hands-on 9
-----------
Delete Country
- Deleted a country using deleteById().
- Verified deletion in MySQL database.

